2 CONC t: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: auto; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration: none; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000;" data-start="1567" data-end="1938">I have been home f
2 CONC ive times since 1907, and Mother came over here in 1910, and we got married on ≤strong data-start="1664" data-end="1681">June 16, 1910≤/strong>, in Edmonton. When I was at home in 1907 and 1908, I spotted a nice girl standing in t
2 CONC he door of a bakery store, and the smile as I went by I never forgot, and I had to go around about to get acquainted&mdash;but finally, I made it. She was the queen of the day.≤/p>400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: auto; text-a
