2 CONC t year. We didn&rsquo;t make enough to pay for our board. That winter the two of us had to go out and work.In March, the man we worked for went broke. We had a few cows, three oxen, and a pony. Second year on the farm we had bad l
2 CONC uck again. I hired out for our neighbor, and Mother, with her first child, Amelia, stayed with my cousin who was neighbor of the man I worked for. His name was Walter Stevens. I went home every night and back to work six o&rsquo;c
