2 CONC olor: #000000; color: #000000;" data-start="2947" data-end="3298">In 1912 we got a pretty good start, and also 1913 and 1914. In the spring of 1914, I put in a crop and was going to the old country that year. I put inthe crop, and
2 CONC  in the summer I rented out the place to two English boys to move on after the crop was taken off. The last part of July, the First World War started, and we could not leave the country.≤/p>normal; widows: auto; word-spacing: 0px;
2 CONC  -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration: none; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000;" data-start="3300" data-end="3536">By this time, we had two children, Amelia and Theodor Johan, and in 1915 the war was going on all ove
2 CONC r. We got another girl, born ≤strong data-start="3430" data-end="3447">April 5, 1915≤/strong>, Harriet. In 1917 I built a two-story house, as the family was growing every other year.≤/p>text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; whit
