2 CONC l, I clerked in the store for a while, and after that, I took carpenter training for a year or so. But in 1901 and 1902, the times got so bad that three of us went off to the U.S.A. (two friends and myself). I worked on the farm f
2 CONC or two summers in Dakota. My friend Ole Sorenson was together with me from the time we left Norway until he died eight years ago.≤/p>ant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: auto; text-align: start; tex
