2 CONC anada together with Ole in 1903, and we had to put in six months out of the year in order to get the land&mdash;one quarter section. My quarter was the S.E. of 30-48-12, west of the 4th Meridian.≤/p>eight: 400; letter-spacing: nor
2 CONC mal; orphans: auto; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: auto; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration: none; caret-color: #000000; color: #000000;" dat
2 CONC a-start="5454" data-end="5617">In the spring of 1904, I went to Edmonton and got work at the D.R. Fraser Company, and worked in the sawmillevery summer until 1910, when Mother came from Norway.≤/p>rt; text-indent: 0px; text-transf
