2 CONT ≤p style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px Helvetica;">CARL HAFSO≤/p>rway, in 1894, the second youngest son in a family of twelve children. In 1911 he left for Canada to join his older brothers Sivert, Tollak and Nels
2 CONC .≤/p>nt: 12.0px Helvetica;">Settling in the Maple Lodge District, he began farming on a homestead he bought half a mile east of the Maple Lodge School. As a janitor at the school in 1926, he made the substantial wage of seven doll
2 CONC ars per month. Carl enjoyed curling with neighbours at the Maple Lodge rink and always made sure the coffee was on for the curlers.≤/p>0px; font: 12.0px Helvetica;">When World War Il started in 1939, Carl joined the air force as a
2 CONC  cook at the base in Cal-gary. Following his air force service, he returned to Viking to farm for a few more years before moving into town around 1952. After moving to town, he worked as a carpenter on a variety of projects, one o
2 CONC f which was the construction of an addition to the original hospital in 1952-53.≤/p>t many crafts including cooking and baking, carpentry, mechanics, black-smithing, and sewing.≤/p>d, Jewell, Brent, Janice, Gerald.≤/p>ont: 12.0px 
2 CONC Helvetica;">Keri Louise, Chelsea Lynn, and Bradley Geoffrey.≤/p>"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px Helvetica;">Golden Valley Lutheran Church.≤/p>n. Taken about 1975.≤/p>e of eighty-three.≤/p>
